],"value":"This enzyme is required for electron transfer from NADP to cytochrome P450 in microsomes (By similarity). It can also provide electron transfer to heme oxygenase and cytochrome B5 (By similarity). Involved in the biosynthesis of the antimalarial endoperoxide artemisinin (PubMed:16612385). Acts as a redox partner for CYP71AV1 which catalyzes the conversion of amorphadiene to more oxygenated products (PubMed:16612385)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"CATALYTIC ACTIVITY","reaction":{"name":"2 oxidized [cytochrome P450] + NADPH = 2 reduced [cytochrome P450] + NADP(+) + H(+)","reactionCrossReferences":[{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA:24040"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:14627"},{"database":"Rhea","id":"RHEA-COMP:14628"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:15378"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:55376"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57783"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58349"},{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:60344"}],"ecNumber":"1.6.2.4","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16612385"}]}},{"commentType":"COFACTOR","cofactors":[{"name":"FAD","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"cofactorCrossReference":{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:57692"}}],"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"value":"Binds 1 FAD per monomer."}]}},{"commentType":"COFACTOR","cofactors":[{"name":"FMN","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"cofactorCrossReference":{"database":"ChEBI","id":"CHEBI:58210"}}],"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"value":"Binds 1 FMN per monomer."}]}},{"commentType":"BIOPHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES","kineticParameters":{"michaelisConstants":[{"constant":4.3,"unit":"uM","substrate":"cytochrome P450","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16612385"}]},{"constant":23.0,"unit":"uM","substrate":"NADPH","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16612385"}]}]}},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"value":"Endoplasmic reticulum membrane","id":"SL-0097"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"value":"Single-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9904"},"orientation":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255","source":"HAMAP-Rule","id":"MF_03212"}],"value":"Cytoplasmic side","id":"SL-9910"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"30851440"}],"value":"Present in non-glandular trichome cells"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"32405226"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"32514287"}],"value":"Artemisinin and derivatives (e.g. artesunate), are antimalarial drugs due to their endoperoxidase properties; they also display multiple pharmacological actions against inflammation,viral infections, and cell and tumor proliferation (PubMed:32405226, PubMed:32514287). Artesunate may be a promising treatment for COVID-19 mediated by the severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (2019-nCoV) (SARS-CoV-2) because of its anti-inflammatory activity, NF-kappaB (nuclear factor kappa B)-coronavirus effect and chloroquine-like endocytosis inhibition mechanism (PubMed:32405226, PubMed:32514287)"}],"commentType":"BIOTECHNOLOGY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16612385"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22247290"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23575629"}],"value":"Yeast (S.cerevisiae) has been engineered to produce artemisinic-acid, a precursor of the antimalarial artemisinin compo